  "text_sanskrit": "किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रिणं च तेजोराशिं सर्वतो दीप्तिमन्तम् । पश्यामि त्वां दुर्निरीक्ष्यं समन्ताद् दीप्तानलार्कद्युतिमप्रमेयम् ॥ ११-१७ ॥",
  "itrans": "kirITinaM gadina.n chakriNa.n cha tejorAshi.n sarvato dIptimantam . pashyAmi tvA.n durnirIkShya.n samantAd.h dIptAnalArkadyutimaprameyam .. 11-17 ..",
  "translation": "With diadem, mace, and discus, mass of splendour, shining everywhere, Thee I behold-Thee dazzling the sight, radiant on all sides like the blazing fire and sun, (yet) unmeasurable. \nV. Yet unmeasurable: this epithet removes the idea of finiteness shadowed by the simile before it.",
